{
  "name": "lifecycle-map",
  "kind": "flow",
  "title": "From plan to operate",
  "desc": "The development lifecycle with devkit, stage by stage, with the command and skill for each: plan with dev plan new and Superpowers; track the task with dev task; build with dev progress and the required skills; pass the local test gate with dev ci --run and dev sec scan; open the PR with dev pr create and the communicating templates; integrate on one branch and push once with dev push; release by the recorded policy with dev release and the release-policy skill; follow CI with dev ci status; deploy through a tag and its pipeline; and hand off with the handoff skill and dev lesson. Each stage feeds the next, so there is no gap between plan and operate.",
  "equal_widths": "all",
